# The ignore file for `Containerfile.freebsd.ingest`, and it is deliberately NOT at the
# repository root.
#
# buildah has no equivalent of BuildKit's `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` lookup, so
# unlike `Containerfile.linux.dockerignore` this one is not found by being
# beside the Containerfile: it is passed explicitly, and the workflow does so.
#
#   buildah bud --ignorefile server/oci/Containerfile.freebsd.ingest.containerignore ...
#
# It could have gone at the context root under the name `.containerignore`,
# which is what buildah looks for there.  It does not, for the reason
# `Containerfile.linux.dockerignore` gives: a test in `usage/tests/test_all.py`
# walks the repository root for container files by NAME and refuses them, on
# the grounds that a root-level container file "reads as the way to run the
# project".  `.containerignore` is not on that test's list today -- which makes
# putting one there a way of satisfying the letter of a guard while defeating
# it, and this repository has audited itself for exactly that shape more than
# once.
#
# The context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because the image needs `server/srv/`,
# `server/oci/` and the staged FreeBSD tree, and no one of them is a parent of
# the others.
#
# Last match wins, so the `__pycache__` line at the bottom is what keeps a
# developer's stale byte-code out of a published image -- and it matters more
# here than it does for Linux, because this image has no RUN and therefore
# never re-compiles what it copies.
# WHAT THIS CONTEXT CONTAINS, NAMED RATHER THAN SWEPT IN.
#
# `!/server/oci/**` used to re-include the whole directory, which was harmless
# while there was one staged tree.  There are four now -- one per component,
# hundreds of megabytes each -- and a context that carried all of them would
# ship the other three trees to this build for no reason.  Named explicitly
# instead, which also means the STAGE build-arg and this file are a pair: build
# with `--build-arg STAGE=somewhere-else` and the COPY fails by name, which is
# the loud half of the trade.
#
# `srv/mcp.py` IS in this context, and that is now unconditional rather than
# provisional.  `srv/serve.py` no longer imports it -- `POST /mcp` moved to the
# mcp component, which is its own image -- but the module still ships with the
# package, because excluding one file from a `COPY server/srv/` would need a
# second COPY list and a list is a place to forget.  What matters is that
# nothing in this image RUNS it: `entrypoint.sh` has no `mcp` mode any more, and
# a test asserts all three of those facts.
*
!/LICENCE
!/server/srv/**
!/server/oci/entrypoint.sh
!/server/oci/preflight.py
!/server/oci/stage-freebsd-ingest/**
**/__pycache__
